ld be improved by  access to more training data all  federated learning is is a really  complicated way of getting access to  more training data so you should only do  it if getting access to more training  data is going to help you don't have to  be doing deep learning I mentioned it a  lot in this talk just because it's you  know hot but you could be using linear  models or SVM's in these approaches as  well  you can't by the way do this approach  federated averaging with trees or  decision forests and the reason for that  is trees are different shapes you can't  meaningfully take the average of two  trees because they're different shapes  so federated averaging won't work there  are other approaches that do work but  out of the box you have to be able to  take the average for federated averaging  to work the two libraries I recommend if  you don't want to implement this stuff  yourself and you don't because  distributed systems and networks are PI  sift intensive flow federated tensorflow  federated art is obviously going to be  where she's you a you should start  you're already in the tensorflow  ecosystem pi sift is an independent  open-source project I like and then you  know the upside downside of working on a  field that doesn't really kind of work  here or has a lot of open problems is  you should read papers and I'm gonna  finish by showing a bunch of papers that  I think you might enjoy reading there's  a couple of blog posts there one we  wrote cloud era is at the top that's  kind of a high-level summary of this  talk the party popper next to the  Federation for Firefox one is because I  particularly recommend that if you  google these you'll bear the first  result or if you DuckDuckGo these  they're the first result the Firefox one  is great it's the most detailed  practical blog post about the networking  and distributed systems issues florian  Hartmann sort of piggybacks on the  telemetry system that already exists in  Firefox to use that to handle the  network traffic it's also interesting  because it uses an SVM rather than a  neural network which is you know always  nice to see people rocking it old-school  the papers they're all good but the  party poppers are next to the the  federated averaging paper and then the  PI sift paper the people that introduces  that I'll tweet a link to these slides  but there's a there is again thank you  very much that's it  [Applause]
 

